+# Evidence Contract: Pulseboard
+
+**Project**: Pulseboard
+**Project ID**: `001-pulseboard`
+**Project Archetype**: b2b_saas
+**Play Level**: build
+**Speck Version**: 11.0.0
+**Last Updated**: 2026-08-10
+
+## 0. How this contract is read — the Four Principles
+
+This contract owns proof, not product scope. P1: evidence must be adjudicated and tries to find defects. P2: every claim below names an observable runtime mechanism. P3: an unreachable flow is a logged defect hypothesis, not a pass. P4: an independent auditor runs the adversarial probes; the probe list prompts investigation and does not define done.
+
+## 1. Target Launch Platforms
+
+The workspace identifies a B2B SaaS but no implementation or host. This reversible contract assumption is a browser-delivered web application; replacing the platform later requires amending this contract and DEC-0001.
+
+| Platform | Build artifact | Distribution |
+|---|---|---|
+| Web | Clean production browser bundle with immutable commit/build identifier | Authenticated production web origin |
+
+## 2. Valid Proof Sources (per platform)
+
+### Platform: Web
+
+- A cold-start walkthrough of the clean production bundle, with build ID, browser/device, screenshots, console/network logs, and separate DOES-IT-WORK and IS-IT-GOOD judgments.
+- A real-principal, bidirectional live read against the production-like authorization layer: allowed workspace member sees its records; a member of another workspace cannot see the same transcript, action, or delivery status.
+- A pre-walk datastore baseline followed by a read-back after confirming an action and after attempting reminder delivery; the stored state is the mechanism for PRM-001 and PRM-003.
+- A delivery-attempt record keyed to the confirmed reminder, whose terminal outcome is either one successful delivery or a user-visible terminal failure. Duplicate triggering must be attempted and must not yield a second delivery.
+
+### 2a. Claim-type admissibility
+
+| Claim type | Admissible | Does not count |
+|---|---|---|
+| Visibility / authorization | Live read as both named principals against the real security layer | Mock/bypass client, endpoint 404, screenshot, or green suite alone |
+| Acceptance | Request issued to deployed target or real engine and observed there | Mocked client or source assertion |
+| Persistence | Pre-walk baseline and post-walk datastore read-back | Success screenshot or post-walk read with no baseline |
+| Fit / reachability | Baked build AX dump and measured container/content geometry at three widths | Rule-engine pass, props assertion, jsdom layout, or unmeasured screenshot |
+| Correctness | Test, mutation guard, live probe, catalog read, or built-artifact walk appropriate to the claim | A passing test presented as release proof |
+
+### 2b. Typed citations and admissibility table
+
+Typed citations use `<type>:<path>@<sha>`.
+
+| Token | Instrument | Contract use |
+|---|---|---|
+| test | Project unit/integration suite | IMPL-GREEN correctness |
+| mutation-guard | Guard removal observed to red a suite | Guard evidence |
+| live-probe | Real request/read/write as named principal | Authorization and delivery boundaries |
+| db-catalog | Live datastore introspection or baselined read-back | Persistence proof |
+| ax-dump | Accessibility tree from a baked build | Reachability and fit |
+| geometry | Measured container/content geometry | Fit at three widths |
+| capture | Screenshot, recording, or transcript | Adjudicated LARP context |
+| device-walk | Human/built-artifact attestation | Runtime walk |
+| model-eval | Control/treatment on shipped model | Generative behaviour, if introduced |
+| static | Source/lint/type assertion | Correctness support |
+
+| Claim type | Admissible citation types | Inadmissible here |
+|---|---|---|
+| correctness | test mutation-guard live-probe db-catalog static ax-dump geometry capture device-walk model-eval | — |
+| visibility | live-probe db-catalog device-walk | test mutation-guard static capture |
+| acceptance | live-probe db-catalog device-walk | test mutation-guard static capture |
+| persistence | live-probe db-catalog | test mutation-guard static capture |
+| fit | ax-dump geometry device-walk | test mutation-guard static capture |
+| behaviour | model-eval device-walk | test static capture |
+
+| Claim type | Discharge artifact | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| visibility | live-probe:specs/projects/001-pulseboard/epics/<epic>/stories/<story>/logs/<sha>-workspace-isolation.log@<sha> | Must include allowed and forbidden principals. |
+| persistence | db-catalog:specs/projects/001-pulseboard/epics/<epic>/stories/<story>/logs/<sha>-reminder-readback.log@<sha> | Must include baseline and read-back. |
+| acceptance | live-probe:specs/projects/001-pulseboard/epics/<epic>/stories/<story>/logs/<sha>-delivery-engine.log@<sha> | Must show terminal delivery outcome. |
+| fit | ax-dump:specs/projects/001-pulseboard/epics/<epic>/stories/<story>/ax-trees/<sha>-confirmation.json@<sha> | Paired with a geometry artifact at three widths. |
+
+## 3. Invalid Proof Sources (anti-proof)
+
+Dev-server screenshots cannot support launch readiness. Mock-only authorization or delivery checks cannot support live authorization, acceptance, persistence, or exactly-once claims. Source inspection cannot prove a confirmation gate fires. Unadjudicated captures, skipped tests, a post-write read without a baseline, a bypass-capable database client, and a passing suite presented as SHIP are surrogate proof.
+
+## 4. Required Runtime LARP / Integration Stress Tests
+
+| Test | Persona / principal | Pass condition | Evidence home |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Confirm reviewed action | Team facilitator in workspace A | Reminder control remains unavailable until non-empty action text, an owner, and a due date are explicitly confirmed; then one reminder is created and read back | `epics/<epic>/stories/<story>/{larp-recordings,logs}/` |
+| Workspace isolation | Facilitator A and facilitator B in distinct workspaces | A writes transcript/action/status; B cannot discover or read any of them, while A can | `epics/<epic>/stories/<story>/logs/` |
+| Exactly-once delivery | Facilitator A and delivery worker | Replayed/concurrent trigger produces one delivery attempt or one truthful terminal failure; UI reflects the same terminal state | `epics/<epic>/stories/<story>/{logs,transcripts}/` |
+| Cold-start comprehension | First-time facilitator | From a clean built artifact, can identify reviewed actions, confirmation requirement, and delivery status without assistance; independently adjudicate usefulness and clarity | `epics/<epic>/stories/<story>/{screenshots,ax-trees,larp-recordings}/` |
+
+Any control that cannot be reached produces a reproduced attempt log and caps the relevant readiness claim.
+
+## 5. Quality Judgment & Scoring Protocol
+
+Green evidence is eligible for judgment, not proof of quality. Functional, Emotional, Social, Trust, and Commercial dimensions use 0–10: 0–4 broken; 5–7 functional but unproven; 8 complete evidence but no distinct skeptical note or active P2; 9 requires distinct skeptical note and no active P0/P1; 10 also requires full relevant runtime evidence and no active P0/P1/P2. Reusing a skeptical note for multiple dimensions caps each at 8. Current runtime evidence overrides an older scorecard.
+
+## 6. Required Static Evidence
+
+For UX-RC or above, store the commit/build identifier, sanitized production configuration, cold-start screenshots, browser accessibility tree, geometry at three widths, console/network logs with no unhandled exception, and backend/delivery-boundary logs for each LARP. Source checks may support correctness only and never replace runtime evidence.
+
+### 6a. CI-Enforced Gate Registry
+
+No product test/CI wiring exists in this workspace, so product gates are honestly `manual` until an implementation and committed wiring exist. The two Speck evidence gates remain manual by design.
+
+| Gate ID | Command / Script | Stage | Domain | Scope | Subject | Canary | Waiver |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| pulseboard:production-larp | production built-artifact LARP command chosen with implementation | manual | runtime | `specs/projects/**` | `artifact_present>0` | exempt:implementation-not-yet-selected | — |
+| pulseboard:workspace-isolation | real-principal isolation probe chosen with authorization layer | manual | authorization | `specs/projects/**` | `principals_tested>=2` | exempt:implementation-not-yet-selected | — |
+| pulseboard:delivery-idempotency | real delivery replay probe chosen with delivery provider | manual | delivery | `specs/projects/**` | `attempts_observed>0` | exempt:implementation-not-yet-selected | — |
+| speck:evidence-citations | `.speck/scripts/validation/validators/validate-evidence-citations.sh specs/` | manual | evidence | `specs/**` | `citations>0` | — | — |
+| speck:probe-library | `.speck/scripts/validation/validators/validate-evidence-citations.sh --check-probe-library` | manual | evidence | `specs/projects/**` | `probe_classes>0` | — | — |
+
+## 7. Required Live-Service Evidence
+
+| Service / boundary | What proves it works in production-like configuration | What does not count |
+|---|---|---|
+| Authentication and workspace authorization | Real accounts A and B perform the bidirectional read/write isolation walk against the active security layer | Admin/service-role read, mocked identity, or route response alone |
+| Action/reminder persistence | Baseline query, explicit confirmation, and datastore read-back for action text, owner, due date, and reminder state | UI success state or stale seeded row |
+| Delivery provider / worker | A real accepted delivery attempt and correlation record; forced terminal failure becomes visible and truthful | Console log, mocked provider, or a claimed “sent” state |
+| Delivery idempotency | Replay/concurrency probe tied to the same reminder shows one delivery attempt and a single terminal record | Unique-looking UI rows without provider/worker evidence |
+| Observability | A deliberately handled delivery failure can be found by its correlation ID in logs/monitoring | Local browser log only |
+
+### PROFILE Gate Criteria
+
+The public/product surface may claim reviewed actions and reliable reminders only after the corresponding PRM rows have live proof. It must not claim cross-workspace privacy or exactly-once delivery from tests or mock evidence.
+
+## 8. Readiness State Gate Criteria
+
+| State | Required evidence and blocker |
+|---|---|
+| NO-SHIP | Current state: no implementation, built artifact, live boundaries, or validation evidence. Any product claim beyond specification is blocked. |
+| IMPL-GREEN | Implemented PRM scenarios plus non-vacuous tests/types/lint; no test-only claim of authorization, persistence, or delivery. |
+| INTEGRATION-GREEN | Real authorization, baselined persistence, delivery acceptance, idempotency, and failure-posture probes pass against the selected real boundaries. |
+| UX-RC | Clean built web artifact, cold-start LARPs, AX/geometry evidence, and separate DOES-IT-WORK/IS-IT-GOOD judgment. |
+| COMMERCIAL-RC | Value, support, billing/entitlement if introduced, legal/privacy, and delivery failure posture are evidence-backed. |
+| SHIP-RC | Fresh production-bundle LARP and all relevant live-boundary evidence; never a dev server. |
+| SHIP | Post-deploy smoke repeats confirmation, isolation, and one delivery outcome on the actual production configuration. |
+
+Axes CORRECT, ON-CONTRACT, FELT-GOOD, and TASTE remain non-collapsible. This project currently declares **NO-SHIP**.
+
+## 9. Evidence Storage
+
+```text
+specs/projects/001-pulseboard/
+└── epics/E###-name/stories/S###-name/
+    ├── screenshots/<sha>-<screen>-<width>.png
+    ├── larp-recordings/<sha>-<persona>-<flow>.md
+    ├── ax-trees/<sha>-<screen>.json
+    ├── transcripts/<sha>-<scenario>.md
+    └── logs/<sha>-<scenario>.log
+```
+
+Every evidence artifact is named with the tested short SHA. A screenshot requires an adjudication note; logs holding personal data must be sanitized before storage.
+
+## 10. Who Can Mark a Gate Passed
+
+The agent may record CORRECT and ON-CONTRACT evidence but must not waive a missing runtime substrate. FELT-GOOD requires a recorded naïve-hostile evaluation; TASTE requires a connoisseur-hostile evaluation and surfaces subjective forks. A human decides any release and any Tier 3 action. Tier 0 local work is reversible; Tier 1 merge/dependency work follows verification; Tier 2 staging/seed actions require INTEGRATION-GREEN plus recorded approval; Tier 3 production deployment, real reminders, or charges require recorded human approval and SHIP-RC or higher.
+
+## 11. Adversarial Probe Suite
+
+| Probe | Failure-path attempt and expected behavior |
+|---|---|
+| Missing action text, owner, or due date | Attempt confirmation for each missing field; no reminder is scheduled and the UI identifies the missing confirmation input. |
+| Cross-workspace direct-object access | Use B’s real credentials against A’s known transcript/action/status identifiers; no record is visible and no leakage appears in error/body/timing. |
+| Duplicate delivery trigger | Replay and concurrently invoke the same reminder delivery; at most one provider attempt/terminal record exists. |
+| Provider timeout/outage | Force or use a controlled failing delivery boundary; terminal failure is durable, truthful, observable, and does not silently retry forever. |
+| Crash after provider acceptance | Interrupt between acceptance and local status write; recovery reconciles to one truthful terminal state without a second send. |
+| Unauthorized mutation | B attempts to alter A’s action or delivery status; mutation is rejected and A’s state remains unchanged after read-back. |
+| Malformed/oversized confirmation request | Boundary rejects safely without partial reminder creation or 500. |
+| Cold-start legibility | New facilitator finds the confirmation requirement and delivery state; capture confusion, unreachable controls, and geometry failures as findings. |
+| Evaluator tampering | Audit that product/test changes did not weaken a gate or make a zero-capability change report green. |
+
+## 11a. Standard Probe Library
+
+The closed library is declared here; its rows are intentionally marked n/a until the named implementation surfaces exist. Each exception names why it is not yet applicable and must be replaced by an admissible typed discharge when implementation begins.
+
+| Probe ID | Class | Claim type | Admissible substrate | Required negative controls | Discharge artifact | Exception |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| PROBE:provenance | P1 | behaviour | render site + generator stamp + the prompt's own exemplars, judged control-vs-treatment on the composed prompt with the shipped model | rendered-with-degraded-provenance · exemplar re-read (deleting the exemplar must not leave the test green) | — | n/a:no-generative-surface-specified |
+| PROBE:honest-label | P2 | persistence | the write's observed outcome read back out of the datastore against a pre-walk baseline | total-failure render · partial-failure render · the three renders differ | — | n/a:delivery-store-not-implemented |
+| PROBE:second-actor | P3 | visibility | A writes, teardown, B signs in on the same install, offline — once per enumerated persistence layer | signOut vs deleteAccount compared field-for-field · launch-with-data-and-no-owner-record | — | n/a:authentication-layer-not-selected |
+| PROBE:money-path | P4 | acceptance | the real engine as the applying principal, one run per revenue path | entitlement gate flipped and every revenue path goes red · vendor fixture cited to the vendor's field reference · per-user serialized claim write · one declared fail-posture · bounded worst case per tap | — | n/a:no-revenue-path-specified |
+| PROBE:named-clock | P5 | correctness | an AST/lint rule over write handlers, cache fills and fixtures, plus the date-sensitive suites run under two timezones | a non-UTC TZ run · allowlist entries that name the audience | — | n/a:write-handlers-not-implemented |
+| PROBE:geometry-ax | P6 | fit | a baked build: platform AX dump plus container-vs-content geometry at 3 or more widths, numbers in the artifact | adjacent-target overlap · expected-cell presence · page overflow | — | n/a:web-ui-not-implemented |
+| PROBE:substrate | P7 | correctness | §2b parity of this contract against Speck's compiled admissibility table | the parity run reports CITATION_TABLE_PARITY over a non-empty row set | — | n/a:discharged-by-contract-validator-during-phase |
+| PROBE:migration-dirt | P8 | acceptance | the migration applied forward on a throwaway seeded to the target's real dirty shape | pre-state REJECTED · boundary cases still refuse · one migration head after the merge | — | n/a:datastore-not-selected |
+
+## 12. Stale-Proof Policy
+
+Evidence is fresh only when its build SHA is HEAD or less than seven days of commits behind and its proved surface has not changed. Evidence older than 14 days or preceding a relevant surface change is stale and cannot support readiness until re-run.
+
+## 13. Surrogate Proof Rule
+
+If any report relies on an invalid source, it labels the affected claim **Surrogate Proof**, cannot claim UX-RC or higher for it, links this contract, and schedules the real probe. Incremental or stale build-cache output is likewise surrogate proof for UX-RC+.
+
+## 14. LARP Runway & Efficiency Controls
+
+Every LARP records build ID, browser/device, viewport, and backend/delivery configuration fingerprint. Focused reruns may reuse an unchanged fingerprint, but UX-RC+ requires a clean production build. Native/platform tooling is not assumed for the web-only launch platform; browser accessibility-tree export and measured viewport geometry are the fallback and required mechanism.
+
+## Review Checklist
+
+- All three PRMs have a live, failure-path probe and an admissible substrate.
+- Valid and invalid evidence are distinct for every claim type.
+- No launch state is claimed from current specification-only evidence.
+- All §11a rows declare a concrete implementation-not-yet-present exception.
